Package: bulkmask
Title: Composition-Adjusted Analysis of Gene-Pair Associations in Bulk RNA-seq
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Hidenori", "Tani", email = "hidenori.tani@yok.hamayaku.ac.jp",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6390-4136"))
Description: A parameterised, reusable pipeline for interpreting bulk-tissue
    RNA-seq when the association between a low-abundance, cell-type-restricted
    regulator and its target may be dominated by shifts in cell composition.
    Given an arbitrary count (or FPKM) matrix, an exposure/outcome gene pair,
    and one or more cell-type marker signatures, the package provides (i)
    per-cohort differential expression (run_de(), DESeq2 with apeglm shrinkage
    or limma-trend; run separately from the pipeline) and a random-effects
    (REML) helper, run_meta(), meant for unshrunken estimates rather than the
    apeglm posterior SDs that run_de() returns for counts; its pipeline runs
    (ii) effector-cell abundance estimation by marker score, xCell raw
    enrichment, and GSVA ssGSEA of the same markers, (iii) partial correlation
    conditioned on the composition estimate(s) and optional nuisance covariates,
    and (iv) a bootstrap decomposition of the observed association into
    composition-associated and residual components (a statistical partition
    under a linear model, not a causal effect). IDI2-AS1 / IL5 across five
    type-2 allergic-disease cohorts is shipped as a worked configuration.
